# Styles

Styles define the shared visual language. Apply the same semantic tokens to native Home Assistant controls, maintained custom cards and documentation examples.

- [Colour roles and accessibility](brand-colour.html): apply colours by purpose, with accessible combinations.
- [Colour palettes](colour.html): choose among ten palettes without changing status meanings.
- [Data visualisation](brand-data.html): choose and compose charts, dashboards and maps.
- [Chart colour](chart-colour.html): generate stable Vivid and Muted series colours, supported by patterns and labels.
- [Typography](typography.html): make labels, values and headings readable.
- [Layout and spacing](layout.html): preserve hierarchy at every width.
- [Icons and images](images.html): use visual recognition with text alternatives.


